Z||000000||Blazin_Low02||09-23-2001||09:38 PM||||Yeah... I have 235/45/R17's for my car for the rear... and 215/45/R17's for the front... what size rims do I need? Is it like... 17x8 for the rear or something? I know 17x7 will work for the front, but I don't want to get the wrong size rims for the rear and have it look goofy or bulge too much. Any help would be greatly appreciated. Thanks.<BR>~James<P>------------------<BR>1986 GT<BR>4 Clicker <BR>White face gauges, blue backlighting, custom marble dash, KYB and Koni, Eibach lowering springs, CD player, Kenwood 4x10's, clarion 4x6 plates, accel coil, aceel race wires, Archie V8 hood scoop, IRM rocker scoops, 1/4 window scoops, and clear tail lights!<P>Soon to have :150 shot of NOS, and a T3 turbo install||||reg||1
Z||000001||Rick 88||09-24-2001||01:13 AM||||17x7's should be fine. I have your same front tire size and a 245/45/17's on the back. My wheels are 17x7.5's all around with a .40 offset. If you find a 7 and 8 combo, that would be nice. I think you would pay more than you really need to get this set up.<P>Are your Eibach springs progressively wound?<BR>I understand these ride better than standard rate lowering springs.<P>Rick<BR>yellow 88 GT 5-speed||||reg||1
